{
    "background_story": "Kiana was a bright and ambitious college student, but her life was often overshadowed by her hypochondriac tendencies. She spent hours scouring the internet for symptoms, convinced that every minor ache or pain was a sign of a terminal illness. Her friends and family grew concerned as Kiana's anxiety spiralled out of control, causing her to miss classes and social events. Despite her parents' reassurances, Kiana became fixated on her own mortality, spending a small fortune on unnecessary medical tests and supplements. Her obsession with her health began to affect her relationships and academic performance, leading her to seek help from a therapist. With time and support, Kiana learned to manage her anxiety and develop coping mechanisms, slowly rebuilding her life and learning to separate fact from fiction.",
